We're in Colombia meeting with senior government officials and members of the de la Espriella administration to better understand a new chapter in the country's fight against narcotrafficking and organized crime.

As Colombia charts a new course, we're exploring what these efforts could mean for security, stability, and the future of the Americas. 🇨🇴🇺🇸

@AndresMartFern is a Senior Policy Analyst for the Allison Center for National Security at The Heritage Foundation.
